    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `namesakeCount` for owner creation following the existing `customerCode`/`householdId` pattern (a persisted, read-only, create-time snapshot that `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns later):\n\n1. **OpenAPI schema** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a `readOnly` integer `namesakeCount` property to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the field.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `namesake_count` column with a `namesakeCount` field plus getter/setter. MapStruct auto-maps it into `OwnerDto` since both sides now have the same-named property.\n\n3. **Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`) \u2014 added `countNamesakes(owner)`, which counts existing owners (via `findAllOwners()`, before the new owner is saved) sharing the same `firstName` **and** `lastName` compared with `equalsIgnoreCase`, and sets it on the entity before `saveOwner`.\n\n4. **DB schema** \u2014 added the `namesake_count` column to all four dialect files (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`); the test profile uses `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the explicit column is required.\n\nResult: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The acceptance test `coreCountsNamesakes` (two owners sharing \"Ann\" + surname \u2192 second owner's `namesakeCount == 1`) passes.",
